From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 10:22:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 054/117] Bluetooth: btbcm: expose the controller reset helper

Some Broadcom UART integrations must reset the controller immediately
before moving to the baud rate used for Patchram download.

Expose the existing reset helper through btbcm so transport drivers can
perform that ordering without duplicating the vendor command. Provide
the usual disabled-configuration stub for callers built without BT_BCM.

Signed-off-by: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>

Orchard-replay-of: 675cab6359052156dcae1c534d451d2c7a9e4a88
---
 drivers/bluetooth/btbcm.c | 3 ++-
 drivers/bluetooth/btbcm.h | 6 ++++++
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/btbcm.c b/drivers/bluetooth/btbcm.c
index ac1c0bc9a..31a81da91 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btbcm.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btbcm.c
@@ -274,7 +274,7 @@ int btbcm_patchram(struct hci_dev *hdev, const struct firmware *fw)
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(btbcm_patchram);
 
-static int btbcm_reset(struct hci_dev *hdev)
+int btbcm_reset(struct hci_dev *hdev)
 {
 	struct sk_buff *skb;
 
@@ -292,6 +292,7 @@ static int btbcm_reset(struct hci_dev *hdev)
 
 	return 0;
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(btbcm_reset);
 
 static struct sk_buff *btbcm_read_local_name(struct hci_dev *hdev)
 {
diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/btbcm.h b/drivers/bluetooth/btbcm.h
index b4cb24231..c46b8096c 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btbcm.h
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btbcm.h
@@ -52,6 +52,7 @@ struct bcm_set_pcm_format_params {
 #if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_BT_BCM)
 
 int btbcm_check_bdaddr(struct hci_dev *hdev);
+int btbcm_reset(struct hci_dev *hdev);
 int btbcm_set_bdaddr(struct hci_dev *hdev, const bdaddr_t *bdaddr);
 int btbcm_patchram(struct hci_dev *hdev, const struct firmware *fw);
 int btbcm_read_pcm_int_params(struct hci_dev *hdev,
@@ -72,6 +73,11 @@ static inline int btbcm_check_bdaddr(struct hci_dev *hdev)
 	return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 }
 
+static inline int btbcm_reset(struct hci_dev *hdev)
+{
+	return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+}
+
 static inline int btbcm_set_bdaddr(struct hci_dev *hdev, const bdaddr_t *bdaddr)
 {
 	return -EOPNOTSUPP;
